  "reason": "The top-3 results (config_029: 0.7250, config_008: 0.7207, config_023: 0.7131) all share scvi_n200 + transformer + multiprofile + multimodal, with variation only in image encoder and fusion. Notably, config_023 (resnet50, weighted) achieves the highest F1 (0.6945) despite slightly lower accuracy, suggesting resnet50 captures complementary information. config_022 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is the only untested configuration that preserves all four winning attributes while testing the resnet50+concat pairing. This clarifies whether the resnet50 F1 advantage is fusion-specific or general, and whether concat might better exploit resnet50's feature space. With only one experiment remaining after this, this is the highest-value exploration in the immediate neighborhood of the current best, as all other untested configs deviate more substantially (worse RNA encoder, avgpool, or singleprofile) and are unlikely to surpass 0.7250."
